30,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have all received our information. I must admit, I am a little concerned about the current state of our staffing and the workload in the lab. I hope we can be mindful of this.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Staffing is one thing, but logistical failures are what truly damage our reputation. I've found that shipping cut-offs are frequently missed, leading to delayed openings. We cannot afford another season of apologies at the door.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"Logistics are boring, Shion! What really matters is the magic. I've seen that people crave movement and human interaction. If a gallery is just a room of silent boxes, they won't come back for a second look.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, movement can be problematic. The maintenance logs show frequent failures with powered displays, often requiring the bay to be roped off. We should be cautious about choosing an exhibition that relies too heavily on complex machinery.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, that sounds like a disaster! But listen, I found something super fishy! The money for shipping and fancy mounts is just disappearing! We're spending way too much on things that aren't even the art!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, please do not be too distressed. I am sure there is a reasonable explanation for the costs. However, we must remember that the people managing those costs are likely very tired.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, fatigue is an excuse, not a solution. @Sakura, the costs are high because we are inefficient. If we choose a proposal with overly complex shipping requirements, we are simply inviting another logistical failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're such a killjoy! Efficiency is fine, but a museum isn't a warehouse. If we're too scared of a little chaos, we'll just end up with a boring show that nobody visits twice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, it is not about being scared, but about reliability. Beyond the machinery, the structural survey shows the suspended bay has a strict weight limit. We cannot risk a proposal that exceeds our physical capacity.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, weight limits are scary! But @Shion, you're right about the inefficiency! I found out that custom mounts are getting way more expensive. We should pick something that brings its own stands to save money!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shizue,,It is a bit worrying to hear about the weight limits and the costs. I only wish we could find a balance that doesn't place too much burden on our few remaining staff members.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, balance is achieved through logic, not hope. We need a proposal with minimal shipping complexity and low weight. If we ignore the data to chase ""magic,"" we are simply planning for failure.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shion, your ""logic"" is just a recipe for a ghost town! If we only prioritize what's easy, we'll lose our audience. We need something that breathes and engages, or we're just wasting the space.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, engagement is important, but not at the cost of the building's integrity. If we ignore the weight limits or the failure rate of powered displays, we risk closing the gallery entirely during the exhibition.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@May, I want magic too! But maybe we can have magic that doesn't break the floor or eat all our pennies? Let's find something that's super cool but comes with its own furniture!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I believe we are all seeing different pieces of the same puzzle. Let us be gentle with one another and keep our tired staff in mind as we review the candidates.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, gentleness doesn't fix a broken schedule. We must prioritize a proposal that is logistically sound. If the paperwork is a mess and the shipping is risky, no amount of kindness will save the opening day.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're still talking about paperwork while the visitors are yawning! Let's stop worrying about the ""how"" for one second and focus on the ""why."" We need a show that actually draws a crowd!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"The ""why"" is irrelevant if the ""how"" is impossible. We cannot ignore the physical reality of the building. Let's ensure the candidates we consider are compatible with our weight limits and technical stability.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, @Shion, you're both so serious! But @May is right, it has to be fun! Let's just look for a candidate that's exciting, light, and doesn't cost a mountain of money for mounts!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shion"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
52,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
