55,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at these options, I feel Option A would be most wonderful. It uses local craftspeople and recorded interviews, which would be much kinder to our exhausted staff and the lab.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, local sources certainly reduce shipping risks. Option A is logically the safest choice. Option D is a logistical nightmare waiting to happen, and Option C's rigging and power needs are far too risky.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shion, ""safest"" is just another word for ""boring""! Option A is okay, but Option B is where the real magic is. A working conservation bench? That's exactly the human interaction people crave!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, Option B involves municipal digs, which often include heavy stonework or soil samples. Given the weight limits of the suspended bay, we must be very careful. Option A is the most structurally sound.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@May, a conservation bench sounds like a cool secret base! But @Shizue and @Misaki are right, Option A seems super safe. Does it come with its own stands? I hope it's not too boring!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shizue"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, I believe the local craftspeople can help us with the displays, which would be a lovely way to involve the community without stressing our staff. It feels like a very peaceful choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, community involvement is a pleasant side effect, but the primary advantage is the elimination of international shipping cut-offs. Option A removes the risk of delayed openings entirely. It is the only rational choice for a stable season.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're treating this like a logistics exam! Option B isn't just ""magic,"" it's a guaranteed draw. People want to see the process, not just the result. A working bench is a magnet for repeat visitors!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a working bench is a draw, but Option B's heavy finds could exceed our weight limits. Option C is even worse; the overhead rigging and power needs are a recipe for the failures I saw in the logs.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, rigging sounds like it would cost a fortune in joiner's fees! @May, I love the bench idea, but if it's too heavy, the floor goes *boom*! Option A is safe, but is it too quiet?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, it may be quiet, but there is a gentle beauty in that. More importantly, Option B's working bench would only add more pressure to our already overwhelmed conservation lab. We must be mindful of their burden.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, exactly. Option B is a contradiction; it invites the public to watch a lab that is already drowning in a backlog. It is an invitation to failure. Option A is the only choice that aligns with our actual capacity.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're just trying to make everything sterile! @Shizue, I hear you, but a dead gallery is a bigger failure. Option A has demonstrations, which is a start, but Option B is a real experience! Let's be bold for once!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, boldness is not a substitute for stability. Option B risks the floor and the lab, and Option C risks the power grid. Option A is the only proposal that respects the building's physical limits.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@May, I want to be bold too, but not ""break the floor"" bold! Option A has demonstrations, which is like a live show! Plus, local stuff means no scary shipping bills. I'm voting for A!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Sakura. Option A is a gentle choice that honors our community and, most importantly, protects our precious staff from further exhaustion. I shall cast my vote for Option A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@May, boldness without a plan is just negligence. Option A is the only choice that guarantees a timely opening and a stable operation. I will not gamble with our reputation. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,May,,"You're all so terrified of a little risk that you're choosing the path of least resistance! But fine, if you're all determined to be boring, I'll cave. At least A has those demonstrations. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"The physical risks associated with the other options are simply too high. To ensure the gallery remains functional and safe for everyone, I must prioritize stability. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"Everyone is agreeing on A! It's a win-win! We get a live show, the floor stays in one piece, and we save all those pennies! I'm super happy! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
